# English additions, loaded on top of tbl/jp.tbl (rombuild.en_table()): later lines win for decoding, and every
# character still encodes. Glyphs: font/en_glyphs.txt (tools/font.py). A-Z (A2-BB) and 0-9 (C6-CF) keep their
# jp.tbl codes and are redrawn; lowercase and punctuation take the hiragana codes 52-78, because the menu-name
# sprite charset only holds codes 01-CF (docs/re/text.md §Font, docs/decisions.md). D0-F6 stay unused.
BF=+
C0=?
C1=!
C2=~
52=a
53=b
54=c
55=d
56=e
57=f
58=g
59=h
5A=i
5B=j
5C=k
5D=l
5E=m
5F=n
60=o
61=p
62=q
63=r
64=s
65=t
66=u
67=v
68=w
69=x
6A=y
6B=z
6C=.
6D=,
6E='
6F="
70=-
71=:
72=;
73=(
74=)
75=&
76=/
77=%
78=…
